I’m rejecting this ticket, as there does not seem to be any issues with caching.

I think that the behaviour Michał experienced is _not_ related to the browser cache but to how the deployments are implemented: the Jenkins pipeline does _not_ actually deploy anything - it _just_ leads to merging a PR with the docker image id, which is then read from the {{master}} branch by the _GitOps (Flux)_ tooling which installs the new image, and this causes some delay. There’s even a note about it at the top of [the document|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4910318240/Builder+Release+Process]:

{quote}Pleaase note, that pipeline status in Jenkins doesn’t show exact timing when new version is available for testing. It takes some time until Flux fully does it job.{quote}

Why don’t I think the browser cache contributes to this? The version of the module that is to be loaded is determined by the {{initrc.js}} file loaded from the server. On every refresh, the file is loaded with a fresh timestamp as a query string, and my browser _never_ indicates loading this file from the cache.I’ve also tried force-full reload of unicorn freshly after a deployment and this does not seem to change a thing. Up until a certain point, I _consistently_ get the _old_ version, whether it’s a forceful reload or not, and from a certain point (which I assume is the point where Flux actually did its job), I get the new content.

I’ve updated the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4910318240/Builder+Release+Process|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ENGINEERING/pages/4910318240/Builder+Release+Process|smart-link] to make it more clear, changing phrases like:

{quote}Then, it merges PR into {{master}} branch, and the manifest changes will be processed by the [https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3722510390/GitOps+Flux|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3722510390/GitOps+Flux|smart-link]  tooling.{quote}

to

{quote}Then, it merges PR into {{master}} branch. The actual deployment of the change will be performed by[https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3722510390|https://taxify.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SRE/pages/3722510390|smart-link] tooling, outside of the Jenkins pipeline - some delay is expected until the changes are propagated.{quote}

