Hello,

{quote}Do you think it could help if I add a new index on (created, city_id, state) ?{quote}


No, not in that order, as range scan (created) should always be the last column in composite index. [https://mysql.rjweb.org/doc.php/index_cookbook_mysql#optimizer_picks_order_by|https://mysql.rjweb.org/doc.php/index_cookbook_mysql#optimizer_picks_order_by|smart-link] . You can try (city_id, event_state,created) instead. 


{quote}Additionally, since the cron now process a single city_id per row, I would like to increase the paralelism. Currently it is 8, would it be a problem if I try with a higher number of parallel threads (let say 10, 15) ? {quote}

Query Resource Units are not too high so I’d say it’s ok to have higher number of parallel threads (please monitor after changing).


