Hello Martyna, 

Thanks for reaching out. I want to clarify:

* *_SD tickets_* _- can you please elaborate on that? Why SD tickets are created? From which team to which? That’s not a part of the Authority requests handling process and agents shouldn’t be doing that._ -{color:#4c9aff} {color}{color:#0747a6}Yes this is not the process and it was rectified by updating the BPO on the correct process last month. {color}

* *_Separation of the process for safety and non-safety authority requests_* _- can you clarify what do you mean by that? Why do you think there’s separation of the process? and_ *Safety and non-safety authority requests* - what exactly do you refer to as safety authority requests and non-safety? Do you mean authority tickets that incorrectly were labeled as Safety tickets, and had to be de-escalated to the non-safety team? _-_  {color:#0747a6}The idea I wish to propose is to approach handling different types of requests, specifically separating non-safety authority-related requests from safety-related issues to improve efficiency.{color}
*# {color:#0747a6}(Non-Safety) Authority Requests: Rides (T1 related){color}
{color:#0747a6}For rides-related authority requests that are non-safety-related (e.g., competition authority requests, non-safety legal summons), we should transition the request from T1 directly to T2 (Ideally very little of this will seep through as the legal team has a mailing address with a particular trigger words that re-direct the non-safety authority emails to their queue). {color}
*# {color:#0747a6}Safety Requests:{color}
{color:#0747a6}For safety-related requests, we propose separating the Beehive flow from Safety-T2-Authority. Instead, these requests should go directly to the Privacy Team, which will help reduce the escalation time from T2. This will result in faster resolutions and improved handling of safety-related issues. Aiming to reduce the Total Resolution Time on the T2 queue. {color}
* *_Unnecessary escalation from T1 to T2 or from safety to the privacy team_* _- why do you think it is unnecessary? The process was created together with the Privacy team and all escalations are needed. -_ {color:#0747a6}In the making of this process the CS team had not transitioned to BPO fully handling the frontline and having the remaining CSS’s transition to market specialists. That means we had enough man-power to handle this as we had an -in-house team that dealt with the issue but with the BPO handling these tickets the suggestion is to have them look into the requests as per the KB which they have access to and after ascertaining the needed info they relay directly to the privacy team without the T2 escalation. {color}

{color:#0747a6}(For KE specifically, the team transitioned fully to BPO handling the frontline queue and the remaining agents becoming market specialists currently we have 5 specialists 2 who handle DEC full time and 3 handling projects and market issues in different capacities with less queue manning time){color}

